[Music]  hi i'm jasmine and today we're going to  be making an epic cheesy volcano fried  rice it's absolutely delicious packed  with flavor it's savory it's spicy  slightly sweet and there's bacon garlic  and cheese so we can't go wrong with  this dish i've already prepped all the  ingredients so let's start cooking  we're going to start by making the fried  rice i'm adding some chopped bacon to my  pan over medium heat and we're gonna  cook it until it's about halfway done  we're gonna let the bacon fat render oh  it smells so good already we can add in  our garlic and our green  onions gotta get every last bit we're  just gonna let that cook for a couple of  minutes so the garlic and the green  onions can soak in the flavor of the  bacon it smells so good i just can't  focus  i can't i can't focus  when i can't  i can't talk  and smell this at the same time once it  looks something like this we can go  ahead and make some space in the middle  and throw in our chopped kimchi  now you can drain your kimchi if you'd  like but because i'm aggressively in  love with the intense flavor of  condensed kimchi juice i will not be  draining it so we're going to cook down  the kimchi until it dries up a little  bit and turns from this vibrant dark red  to a little bit of a reddish brown we  want to make sure that it's well reduced  otherwise once we add in the rice and  the sauce it's just going to be one  soggy wet mess also if you're not a huge  kimchi fan you can reduce the amount of  kimchi in here or even just take it out  completely but if you haven't tried  cooked kimchi i really do recommend that  you try it because it tastes so  different from raw kimchi  free facials  so once your kimchi looks something like  this we're ready to add the sauce and to  make the sauce we're just going to add  in two tablespoons of gochujang which is  korean red pepper paste two tablespoons  of mirin which is sweet rice wine one  tablespoon of soy sauce and one  tablespoon of sesame oil and just give  it a good mix just gonna pour it all  over the kimchi bacon garlic and green  onions i mixed all the sauces first in a  different bowl i think it helps break  down the pepper paste better and mixes  in better but you can add it directly to  the pan if you want perfect let's mix  this up  until it's well combined  wow  the smells are immaculate in my  apartment  yum okay this is coming together so  nicely i'm gonna add in two cups of  leftover rice leftover okay guys  left over rice you can use fresh if you  want to but then don't get mad at me if  your fried rice is wet and soggy use  leftover rice gonna break up the larger  chunks and just get all of this  well incorporated we're gonna cook the  rice for three to four more minutes and  i'm actually gonna let the rice crisp up  on the bottom when my best friends and i  made fried rice in college we would  always let the rice crisp up and then we  would fight for that scorched rice  because the texture is just so  so good it's actually a very popular  snack amongst koreans it's called  nurunji and it's literally just scorched  rice it's  so good  all right y'all this looks about done so  we're gonna turn off the heat and we're  going to transfer this into my volcano  shaped bowl and while i'm a thousand  percent positive that every single one  of you has a volcano shaped bowl in the  off chance that you don't have a volcano  shaped bowl you can just use a small to  medium sized bowl as deep as you can  find this is the bowl i'm using i  usually use this for my noodles and it's  actually the perfect volcano shape let's  carefully transfer all of our fried rice  into the bowl and we're going to press  it down until it's compact  now we're going to safely flip this onto  our new pan your heat should not be on  yet don't burn yourself i'm actually  going to put the pan on top of the fried  rice  and we're going to flip it  okay  give it a little jiggle so it comes out  i'm going to indent the top a little  careful if you press too hard and too  fast it will break apart  i'm getting so excited  why is food so fun  and so good i'm gonna make a fat crevice  over here so we can get a lot of egg and  cheese lava our volcano looks ready for  the egg and cheese lava let's turn our  heat back on  to medium  and it's time for some action baby i  have four whisked eggs in here and i'm  just gonna pour it over our volcano  oh  my god  ah  it looks so good  cheesy goodness guys gonna top it with  mozzarella  and just pour it all over our eggs  if you love cheese you know i'm not  stopping you from adding more  if you want to go the extra mile  sometimes i like to add sweet corn  and it just  food heaven  we're gonna cover our pan just until the  eggs cook through and the cheese melts  avoid overcooking your eggs because we  don't want it to be dry and rubbery we  want it to be light and fluffy  all right guys looks about done this is  the cheesy volcano fried rice a  delicious kimchi fried rice surrounded  in an egg and cheese moat topped with  even more cheese this is a good day  [Music]  moment of silence please  sometimes food just needs  a moment to shine  wow that's so good of course it's not  too different from your average kimchi  fried rice but making it like this is so  fun  i'm gonna invite my boyfriend to try it  george you want to come try this  sure  whoa that is beautiful i kind of ruined  it well i mean it already looks so good  the lot was flowing out you want to try  yes i would love to  good  you did a good job that's so good all  right guys we're going to go ahead and  finish the rest of this if you end up  making the cheesy volcano fried rice  make sure to take a picture and tag me  on instagram and if you want to see more  of my content make sure to subscribe to  bring me bye  guys oh yes  [Music]  you

